        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: కానీ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కానీ (kānī) — \"but\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కానీ (kānī) turns a sentence around. Where మరియు (mariyu) adds, కానీ (kānī) takes back: it warns the listener that what comes next does not match what came before."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నాకు టీ ఇష్టం, కానీ (kānī) పాలు వద్దు — \"I like tea, but no milk.\" This one word is what lets you disagree politely instead of only saying లేదు."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two clauses, and a way to set the second against the first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
